# The words of the window of FreeSynergy Decisions, English (ADR 0057: MessageFormat 2). Every id needs a German twin in de.mf2.
app-name = FreeSynergy Decisions
app-tagline = Goal: Decide together without a detour: proposals and polls with a method the creator fixes before anyone votes, and finding a date by poll; the result is recorded by a person.
soon = coming soon
preview = Preview
state-connected = The server answers and speaks the contract {$contract}.
state-down-unreachable = No server is running ({$detail}).
state-down-timeout = A server holds the socket but does not answer within {$detail} ms.
state-down-protocol = The server answered something this window cannot read ({$detail}).
state-contract = This frontend does not fit the server: it speaks {$found}, this window needs {$expected} (same main level, minor level not lower).
state-hint-down = Start the program with the command fs-decisions; it starts the server and this window.
state-hint-contract = Install a matching version of FreeSynergy Decisions; the window below only shows what is planned.
today-title = What it can do today
today-1 = Opens this window, finds its server and checks that both speak the same contract version.
today-2 = Shows a first look at the main view (page "Decisions"): a date poll grid with participants and time windows, and the list of my decisions, both with example data, marked as a preview; nothing in it is real, nothing is saved or sent.
today-3 = The counting of votes (ten methods, an anonymous ballot box) exists as a library inside fs-forms, not moved out yet and not connected to this window; the server only reports what it offers, which is nothing yet.
coming-title = What comes
coming-1 = Date poll: several time windows (start, duration, zone) or whole days; each person answers Yes, If needed or No per window and may add a comment.
coming-2 = The grid with the three answers kept apart; the suggestion is the window with the most commitments (Yes plus If needed), on a tie the one with fewer "If needed"; the rule stands next to it, "If needed" is not weighted.
coming-3 = Times shown in the zone of each viewer, with the zone of the poll as a label.
coming-4 = A person fixes the date; the invitation and the entry in Calendars follow.
coming-5 = The list of my decisions with title, state and deadline, a search and the filter Open or Decided.
coming-6 = Create a decision: title, proposal text, options, method, deadline and who may vote; the creator fixes the method before the vote and everyone sees it, a group may prescribe a method.
coming-7 = Methods: majority, two thirds, relative majority and approval.
coming-8 = Vote in the window: Yes, No or Abstain, changeable while the vote is open; anonymous or public, chosen when creating and never switched.
coming-9 = The result is recorded by a person and stays after the single votes are deleted; a machine never decides.
coming-10 = Invite people and groups through the person picker; the electorate is fixed when the vote opens.
coming-11 = Single decision with a reason: a decision diary, useful alone.
coming-12 = Automation through workflows, not macros: the commands and objects of Decisions become blocks of the visual workflows, with the rights of whoever starts them.
coming-13 = More, each planned, not scheduled, no promise: points and allocation, ranked methods (Schulze, instant runoff, Borda, STV), consent and systemic consensing, objections and new versions, quorum, deadlines with reminders, guests by link, comparing with your calendar, delegation of votes (decided as later), phases, discussion, export, and the name of the whole date-finding suite (still open).
menu-program = Decisions
menu-new = New decision
menu-poll = New date poll
menu-record = Record result
screen-start = Start
screen-main = Decisions
screen-coming = What comes
status-ready = Ready
m-banner-title = Preview
m-banner-text = These are example data so you can see what Decisions will look like. None of it is real; nothing is saved or sent. Real data appears here as soon as the server provides it.
m-poll-title = Date poll (example)
m-col-people = Participants
m-suggested = suggestion
m-yes = Yes
m-if-needed = If needed
m-no = No
m-sum-yes = Yes (count)
m-sum-if-needed = If needed (count)
m-sum-no = No (count)
m-sum-commitments = Commitments (Yes plus If needed)
m-suggestion = Suggestion: {$window} ({$yes} Yes, {$if} If needed)
m-commitments-spoken = {$count} commitments
m-rule = Rule of the suggestion: the window with the most commitments (Yes plus If needed); on a tie the one with fewer "If needed", then the earliest. "If needed" is not weighted. A person fixes the date; nothing is decided by itself.
m-zone = All times are UTC, the zone of the poll. Later each person sees their own zone.
m-list-title = My decisions (example)
m-col-title = Title
m-col-state = State
m-col-deadline = Deadline (UTC)
m-state-open = Open
m-state-decided = Decided
m-sample-a = Example A
m-sample-b = Example B
m-sample-c = Example C
m-sample-d = Example D
m-sample-poll = Example date poll
m-sample-motion = Example proposal
m-sample-diary = Example single decision
m-empty-title = No decisions yet
m-empty-text = The server offers decisions, but this window cannot read them yet. Nothing is shown instead of invented examples.
